clouddrop (0.3.0~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.3.0 (see CHANGELOG.md).
  * More clouds besides Google Drive: OneDrive, Dropbox, WebDAV, Nextcloud,
    S3-compatible storage, SFTP and MEGA, chosen in the setup assistant.
  * Several folders at once, each uploading to a cloud of its own: a folder
    switcher in the window, the top-bar icon and the Files integration.
  * Appearance settings: light or dark style and an accent colour.
  * New logo and a refreshed window (status card, activity filters, About).
  * The desktop app needs libadwaita 1.5 (GNOME 46) or later.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:14:25 +0530

clouddrop (0.2.0~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.2.0 (adds CloudDrop for Windows; see CHANGELOG.md).
  * Command line: `clouddrop logout`; `status --json` works before setup and
    reports configured, config_error, paused and root_id; `service status
    --json`; `reset-cloud` restarts the service itself.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:06:37 +0530

clouddrop (0.1.0~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Upload-only sync of ~/CloudDrop to Google Drive with the same folder
    structure; local deletes keep the Drive copy (cloud-only).
  * Resumable uploads; renames and moves mirrored without re-uploading.
  * Free Up Space by hand or automatically, with folders kept on this
    computer; frees only after Google Drive's checksum matches.
  * Desktop app (setup assistant, Home, Files, Activity, Settings), top-bar
    status icon, and GNOME Files status icons and actions.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0530
